Hi Johanne,

The guess object is not a statistical estimate, and is supposed to have infinitely wide credible intervals. From your screenshot, all of the point estimates in your guess object are finite values, which is all that you need to provide the initial guess to the optimizer in ctmm.fit() and ctmm.select(). vignette('variogram') walks through this: https://ctmm-initiative.github.io/ctmm/articles/variogram.html and I'll also walk through it during the webinar on Monday.

Best,
Chris

